title: Check configured address identity against the node key
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    `--listen-addr` and `--public-addr` accept a trailing `/p2p/<peer id>`, and a
    `/certhash/<hash>` before it on a `webrtc-direct` address. Both are checked against the node
    key and stripped. The node refuses to start if either does not match, or if the node key does
    not exist yet.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `NetworkConfiguration::validate_and_complete_webrtc_addresses` is renamed to
    `validate_and_complete_addresses`. It now also checks the `/p2p` and `/certhash` components of
    listen and public addresses against the node key and strips them, on both network backends,
    pinning the resolved key into `NetworkConfiguration::node_key`.

    `sc_network::error::Error` gains `MismatchedAddressIdentity`, `MalformedAddressIdentity` and
    `AddressIdentityWithoutNodeKey`.
crates:
- name: sc-cli
  bump: minor
- name: sc-network
  bump: major
